This project aims to analyze employee performance data to uncover key factors influencing productivity and job satisfaction. By leveraging data analysis and machine learning techniques, we strive to provide actionable insights that can aid in strategic decision-making for workforce management.​
🎯 Objectives

    Identify factors affecting employee performance.

    Predict performance ratings based on various attributes.

    Visualize trends and correlations within the dataset.​

🧰 Tools & Technologies

    Programming Language: Python

    Libraries: pandas, numpy, matplotlib, seaborn, scikit-learn

    Environment: Jupyter Notebook

📂 Dataset

Source: IBM HR Analytics Employee Attrition & Performance dataset

Description: Contains various attributes related to employee demographics, job roles, satisfaction levels, and performance metrics.

Download Link: Kaggle Dataset

📝 Project Structure

Employee-Performance-Analysis/
├── data/
│   └── WA_Fn-UseC_-HR-Employee-Attrition.csv
├── notebooks/
│   └── employee_performance_analysis.ipynb
├── src/
│   ├── data_preprocessing.py
│   ├── eda.py
│   ├── modeling.py
│   └── visualization.py
├── outputs/
│   ├── figures/
│   └── models/
├── README.md
└── requirements.txt

🔍 Methodology

    Data Preprocessing:

        Handled missing values and outliers.

        Encoded categorical variables.

        Normalized numerical features.​

    Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA):

        Visualized distributions and relationships between variables.

        Identified correlations and patterns.​

    Modeling:

        Implemented classification models (e.g., Logistic Regression, Random Forest).

        Evaluated model performance using metrics like accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score.​

    Visualization:

        Created plots to illustrate findings and model results
📈 Results

    Key Findings:

        Overtime and job satisfaction significantly impact performance ratings.

        Employees with higher education levels tend to have better performance scores.​

    Model Performance:

        Achieved an accuracy of 85% using the Random Forest class

🚀 Getting Started

    Clone the repository:

git clone https://github.com/Sowmyakari/Employee-Performance-Analysis.git
cd Employee-Performance-Analysis

Install dependencies:

pip install -r requirements.txt

Run the analysis:

jupyter notebook notebooks/employee_performance_analysis.ipynb



